---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Getting Started"
  description="Install OMAR and run programmable agentic workflows."
>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    OMAR provides deterministic orchestration for agentic workflows. Describe a
    task in Mission Control, review the team diagram, and confirm deployment.
  </p>
  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <p>
    Install tmux 3.0+, Git, and at least one supported coding agent: Claude
    Code, Codex CLI, Cursor CLI, OpenCode, Google Antigravity CLI, or Pi.
  </p>
  <h2>Install</h2>
  <h3>One-liner (recommended)</h3>
  <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://omar.rs/install.sh | sh</code></pre>
  <p>
    Supports macOS and Linux; installs omar and omarc to /usr/local/bin by
    default.
  </p>
  <h3>Homebrew</h3>
  <pre><code>brew install omar-os/omar/omar</code></pre>
  <h3>Build from source</h3>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/omar-os/omar.git
cd omar
make install</code></pre>
  <p>
    Requires Rust 1.89+, GNU Make, Node.js 22.13+, and elan. make install builds
    Mission Control and the omarc compiler.
  </p>
  <h2>Launch Mission Control</h2>
  <pre><code>omar up --name dev --web</code></pre>
  <p>
    Start an independent background session and open Mission Control in your
    browser. Describe a workflow, review the generated program, and confirm
    deployment to watch it run. Closing the browser leaves the session running.
  </p>
  <h2>Manage sessions</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr
        ><td><code>omar up --name dev</code></td><td
          >Start a session, or restart the stopped session with this name.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>omar attach -s dev --web</code></td><td
          >Open the session in your browser; use --tui for the terminal UI.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>omar down -s dev</code></td><td
          >Stop the session and keep its state.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>omar rm -s dev</code></td><td
          >Remove the session and its state, stopping it first if running.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr><td><code>omar ls</code></td><td>List sessions.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Use omar --help for commands and omar &lt;command&gt; --help for options.
  </p>
  <h2>Choose a backend</h2>
  <p>
    Choose the backend for a new session’s initial assistant. Add --web or --tui
    to open a client immediately.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Backend</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr
        ><td><code>omar -a claude up --name claude</code></td><td
          >Claude Code</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>omar -a codex up --name codex</code></td><td>Codex CLI</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>omar -a cursor up --name cursor</code></td><td>Cursor CLI</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>omar -a opencode up --name opencode</code></td><td
          >OpenCode</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>omar -a agy up --name agy</code></td><td
          >Google Antigravity CLI</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr><td><code>omar -a pi up --name pi</code></td><td>Pi</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <h2>Terminal UI</h2>
  <pre><code>omar attach -s dev --tui</code></pre>
  <p>
    Attach the terminal dashboard to the same session. Press z to detach and
    leave it running; Q stops the session after confirmation.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .docs-lead {
    color: var(--text-bright);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
</style>
